oint of } S \\text{ and } T.}\n\\]", "ground_truth_solution": "\n1. **Identify Key Angles and Circle $\\omega$:**\n   - Let the angles of the triangle $ABC$ be $\\alpha = \\angle CAB$, $\\beta = \\angle ABC$, and $\\gamma = \\angle BCA$.\n   - The line $AJ$ bisects $\\angle CAB$, so $\\angle JAK = \\angle JAL = \\frac{\\alpha}{2}$.\n   - Because $\\angle AKJ = \\angle ALJ = 90^\\circ$, the points $K$ and $L$ lie on the circle $\\omega$ with diameter $AJ$.\n\n2. **Establish Tangency Properties and Angle Relationships:**\n   - The triangle $KBM$ is isosceles since $BK$ and $BM$ are tangents to the excircle.\n   - The angle bisector $BJ$ bisects $\\angle KBM$, giving $\\angle MBJ = 90^\\circ - \\frac{\\beta}{2}$ and $\\angle BKM = \\frac{\\beta}{2}$.\n   - Similarly, $\\angle MCJ = 90^\\circ - \\frac{\\gamma}{2}$ and $\\angle CML = \\frac{\\gamma}{2}$.\n\n3. **Proving $F$ and $G$ Lie on Circle $\\omega$:**\n   - The angles $\\angle BMF$ and $\\angle CML$ are equal; thus:\n     \\[\n     \\angle LFJ = \\angle MBJ - \\angle BMF = \\left(90^\\circ - \\frac{\\beta}{2}\\right) - \\frac{\\gamma}{2} = \\frac{\\alpha}{2} = \\angle LAJ\n     \\]\n   - Because $\\angle LFJ = \\angle LAJ$, point $F$ lies on circle $\\omega$.\n   - Analogously, we can show that $G$ also lies on $\\omega$.\n   - Since $AJ$ is a diameter of $\\omega$, we have:\n     \\[\n     \\angle AFJ = \\angle AGJ = 90^\\circ\n     \\]\n\n4. **Symmetry and Equality of Segments $SM$ and $TM$:**\n   - The lines $AB$ and $BC$ are symmetric with respect to the external angle bisector $BF$.\n   - Two perpendicular lines to $BF$ are $AF$ and $KM$; thus, $SM$ and $AK$ are symmetric about $BF$, hence $SM = AK$.\n   - Similarly, $TM$ and $AL$ are symmetric about $BF$, hence $TM = AL$.\n   - Since $AK = AL$ (tangents to the excircle), it follows directly that:\n     \\[\n     SM = TM\n     \\]\n   - Therefore, $M$ is the midpoint of $ST$.\n\n### Conclusion:\n\\[\n\\boxed{M \\text{ is the midpoint of } ST}\n\\]", "domain":