1a3)/6\n\nSimilarly, compute centroids for the other sides.\n\nLet's compute centroid \u0394_B, the center of the equilateral triangle on AC.\n\nFollowing the same process, rotate A around C by 60 degrees counterclockwise to get the third vertex E:\n\nE = C + (A - C) * e^{i\u03c0/3}\n\nThen centroid \u0394_B = (A + C + E)/3\n\nSubstituting E:\n\n= (A + C + [C + (A - C)(1/2 + i\u221a3/2)])/3\n\n= [A + C + C + (A - C)(1/2 + i\u221a3/2)] /3\n\n= [A + 2C + (A - C)(1/2 + i\u221a3/2)] /3\n\nSimilarly, expanding (A - C)(1/2 + i\u221a3/2):\n\n= (A/2 - C/2) + i\u221a3/2 (A - C)\n\nThus:\n\n[A + 2C + A/2 - C/2 + i\u221a3/2 (A - C)] /3\n\nCombine terms:\n\nA + A/2 = 3A/2\n\n2C - C/2 = 3C/2\n\nSo:\n\n[3A/2 + 3C/2 + i\u221a3/2 (A - C)] /3\n\nFactor out 3/2:\n\n= [ (3/2)(A + C) + i\u221a3/2 (A - C) ] /3\n\n= (A + C)/2 + (A - C)(i\u221a3)/6\n\nSimilarly, centroid \u0394_C, the center of the equilateral triangle on AB.\n\nThird vertex F constructed by rotating B around A by 60 degrees counterclockwise:\n\nF = A + (B - A) * e^{i\u03c0/3}\n\nCentroid \u0394_C = (A + B + F)/3\n\nSubstituting F:\n\n= (A + B + [A + (B - A)(1/2 + i\u221a3/2)])/3\n\n= [A + B + A + (B - A)(1/2 + i\u221a3/2)] /3\n\n= [2A + B + (B - A)(1/2 + i\u221a3/2)] /3\n\nExpanding (B - A)(1/2 + i\u221a3/2):\n\n= (B/2 - A/2) + i\u221a3/2 (B - A)\n\nThus:\n\n[2A + B + B/2 - A/2 + i\u221a3/2 (B - A)] /3\n\nCombine terms:\n\n2A - A/2 = 3A/2\n\nB + B/2 = 3B/2\n\nSo:\n\n[3A/2 + 3B/2 + i\u221a3/2 (B - A)] /3\n\nFactor out 3/2:\n\n= [ (3/2)(A + B) + i\u221a3/2 (B - A) ] /3\n\n= (A + B)/2 + (B - A)(i\u221a3)/6\n\nNow we have expressions for the three centroids \u0394_A, \u0394_B, \u0394_C:\n\n\u0394_A = (B + C)/2 + (C - B)(i\u221a3)/6\n\n\u0394_B = (A + C)/2 + (A - C)(i\u221a3)/6\n\n\u0394_C = (A + B)/2 + (B - A)(i\u221a3)/6\n\nNow, to show that triangle \u0394 (with vertices \u0394_A, \u0394_B, \u0394_C) is equilateral, we need to show that the distances between each pair of these points are equal.\n\nIn complex numbers, the d