\u221a3 /6 - q/2 )\n\nSquared distance |\u0394_C - \u0394_A|\u00b2:\n\n[ -p/2 + q\u221a3/6 ]\u00b2 + [ (2 - p )\u221a3 /6 - q/2 ]\u00b2\n\nFirst term:\n\n= ( p\u00b2/4 - (p q\u221a3)/6 + (3q\u00b2)/36 )\n\n= p\u00b2/4 - (p q\u221a3)/6 + q\u00b2/12\n\nSecond term:\n\nExpand [ (2 - p )\u221a3 /6 - q/2 ]\u00b2\n\n= [ (2 - p )\u221a3 /6 ]\u00b2 - 2*(2 - p )\u221a3 /6 * q/2 + (q/2 )\u00b2\n\n= ( 3(2 - p )\u00b2 ) /36 - ( (2 - p )\u221a3 q ) /6 + q\u00b2/4\n\n= ( (2 - p )\u00b2 ) /12 - ( (2 - p )\u221a3 q ) /6 + q\u00b2/4\n\nCombine both terms:\n\nFirst term contributions: p\u00b2/4 - (p q\u221a3)/6 + q\u00b2/12\n\nSecond term contributions: (2 - p )\u00b2 /12 - ( (2 - p )\u221a3 q ) /6 + q\u00b2/4\n\nTotal:\n\n= p\u00b2/4 - (p q\u221a3)/6 + q\u00b2/12 + (4 -4p +p\u00b2)/12 - ( (2 - p )\u221a3 q ) /6 + q\u00b2/4\n\nConvert all terms to twelfths:\n\np\u00b2/4 = 3p\u00b2/12\n\n- (p q\u221a3)/6 = -2p q\u221a3/12\n\nq\u00b2/12 remains\n\n(4 -4p +p\u00b2)/12 remains\n\n- ( (2 - p )\u221a3 q ) /6 = -2(2 - p )\u221a3 q /12\n\nq\u00b2/4 =3q\u00b2/12\n\nThus:\n\n= 3p\u00b2/12 -2p q\u221a3/12 + q\u00b2/12 + (4 -4p +p\u00b2)/12 -2(2 - p )\u221a3 q /12 +3q\u00b2/12\n\nCombine like terms:\n\np\u00b2 terms: 3p\u00b2/12 + p\u00b2/12 =4p\u00b2/12 = p\u00b2/3\n\nq\u00b2 terms: q\u00b2/12 +3q\u00b2/12 =4q\u00b2/12 = q\u00b2/3\n\np terms: -4p/12 = -p/3\n\nConstants:4/12 =1/3\n\nCross terms with pq\u221a3:\n\n-2p q\u221a3/12 - (-2(2 - p )\u221a3 q ) /12\n\nWait, let's compute:\n\n-2p q\u221a3/12 -2(2 - p )\u221a3 q /12\n\n= [ -2p q\u221a3 -4\u221a3 q +2p\u221a3 q ] /12\n\n= [ (-2p q\u221a3 +2p\u221a3 q ) -4\u221a3 q ] /12\n\n= [ 0 -4\u221a3 q ] /12\n\n= -4\u221a3 q /12\n\n= -\u221a3 q /3\n\nWait, this seems off. Let me re-examine.\n\nWait, the second term is -2(2 - p )\u221a3 q /12, which is -2*2\u221a3 q /12 +2*p\u221a3 q /12 = -4\u221a3 q /12 +2p\u221a3 q /12 = -\u221a3 q /3 + (p\u221a3 q)/6\n\nBut the first cross term is -2p q\u221a3 /12 = -p q\u221a3 /6\n\nSo total cross terms:\n\n- p q\