umber of 5s in (2d +1)] (from 5b) + 0 (from third number).\n\nTotal 2s = [2 + number of 2s in c] (from 10a) + 0 (from 5b) + [1 + number of 2s in t] (from third number).\n\nOur goal is to maximize min(total 5s, total 2s).\n\nTo maximize this, we need to balance total 5s and total 2s. Let's try to find values of c and d (and hence s) that maximize both.\n\nFirst, note that 2c +5d=97 -s. Since s\u22650, 2c +5d \u226497.\n\nWe can express c in terms of d and s: c=(97 -s -5d)/2.\n\nSince c must be integer, 97 -s -5d must be even. So 97 -s -5d \u22610 mod2 \u21d2s +5d \u226197 mod2 \u21d2s +d \u22611 mod2 (since 97 is odd and 5d\u2261d mod2).\n\nTherefore, s and d must have opposite parity.\n\nNow, let's attempt to choose d and s such that:\n\n1. 2c +5d=97 -s.\n\n2. s \u22650.\n\n3. c \u22650, d \u22650.\n\n4. t=5s +4 must be positive, so 489 -10c -25d >0. But since 2c +5d=97 -s, substituting c=(97 -s -5d)/2:\n\nt=489 -10*( (97 -s -5d)/2 ) -25d=489 -5*(97 -s -5d) -25d=489 -485 +5s +25d -25d=4 +5s.\n\nSo t=5s +4, which matches our earlier result. So as long as s \u22650, t \u22654. So the third number=2t \u22658, which is positive.\n\nTherefore, our main constraint is 2c +5d=97 -s, with c=(97 -s -5d)/2 \u22650, d \u22650, s \u22650, and s +d \u22611 mod2.\n\nTo maximize total 5s and 2s, we need to maximize the number of 5s in c and (2d +1), and the number of 2s in c and t.\n\nLet's first try to maximize the number of 5s.\n\nNumber of 5s:\n\n1 (from 10a) + number of 5s in c\n\n+ 2 (from 5b) + number of 5s in (2d +1)\n\n=3 + number of 5s in c + number of 5s in (2d +1).\n\nSimilarly, number of 2s:\n\n2 (from 10a) + number of 2s in c\n\n+ 1 (from third number) + number of 2s in t\n\n=3 + number of 2s in c + number of 2s in t.\n\nTo maximize the minimum of these two totals, we need to balance them.\n\nLet's first try to maximize the number of 5s.\n\nTo do that, we need c and (2d +1) to have as many factors of 5 as possible.\n\nSimilarly, to maximize the number of 2s, we need c 