ait, let's perform the division properly.\n\nDivide x\u00b2 +1 by -x +1.\n\nDivide x\u00b2 by -x, which gives -x. Multiply (-x +1) by -x: x\u00b2 -x. Subtract from x\u00b2 +1:\n\n(x\u00b2 +1) - (x\u00b2 -x) =x +1. So remainder is x +1.\n\nThen, divide the previous divisor (-x +1) by this remainder x +1.\n\nDivide -x +1 by x +1. The leading term is -x /x =-1. Multiply (x +1) by -1: -x -1. Subtract from (-x +1):\n\n(-x +1) - (-x -1) =2. So remainder is2.\n\nTherefore, the steps are correct. Then, backtracking:\n\n2 = (x\u00b2 +1) - (-x -1)*(-x +1)\n\nBut from step1: (-x +1)=x\u00b3 +1 -x*(x\u00b2 +1)\n\nSubstitute into the above:\n\n2 = (x\u00b2 +1) - (-x -1)*(x\u00b3 +1 -x*(x\u00b2 +1))\n\n= (x\u00b2 +1) + (x +1)(x\u00b3 +1) -x(x +1)(x\u00b2 +1)\n\nTherefore,\n\n2 = (x\u00b2 +1)(1 -x(x +1)) + (x +1)(x\u00b3 +1)\n\nCompute 1 -x(x +1)=1 -x\u00b2 -x\n\nTherefore,\n\n2 = (x\u00b2 +1)(-x\u00b2 -x +1) + (x +1)(x\u00b3 +1)\n\nBut wait, this is different from what I had earlier. Previously, I think I made a mistake in the substitution.\n\nCorrectly, after expanding:\n\n2 = (x\u00b2 +1) + (x +1)(x\u00b3 +1) -x(x +1)(x\u00b2 +1)\n\n= (x\u00b2 +1) -x(x +1)(x\u00b2 +1) + (x +1)(x\u00b3 +1)\n\nFactor (x\u00b2 +1):\n\n= (x\u00b2 +1)(1 -x(x +1)) + (x +1)(x\u00b3 +1)\n\nCompute 1 -x(x +1)=1 -x\u00b2 -x\n\nTherefore:\n\n2 = (x\u00b2 +1)(-x\u00b2 -x +1) + (x +1)(x\u00b3 +1)\n\nThis is the correct equation. Then, writing:\n\n2 = - (x\u00b2 +1)(x\u00b2 +x -1) + (x +1)(x\u00b3 +1)\n\nTherefore, rearranged:\n\n1 = - (1/2)(x\u00b2 +1)(x\u00b2 +x -1) + (1/2)(x +1)(x\u00b3 +1)\n\nThus, the B\u00e9zout coefficients are A(x)= - (1/2)(x\u00b2 +x -1) and B(x)= (1/2)(x +1). Therefore, the solution is P(x)=(x\u00b2 +1)A(x)= - (1/2)(x\u00b2 +1)(x\u00b2 +x -1)\n\nLet me compute this P(x):\n\nFirst, expand (x\u00b2 +1)(x\u00b2 +x -1):\n\n= x\u00b2*(x\u00b2 +x -1) +1*(x\u00b2 +x -1)\n\n= x^4 +x^3 -x\u00b2 +x\u00b2 +x -1\n\nSimplify:\n\n= x^4 +x^3 +0x\u00b2 +x -1\n\nMultiply by -1/2:\n\nP(x)= -1/2 x^4 