.\n   - The sequence \\( x_n \\) starts at \\( \\pi/6 \\) and increments by \\( \\pi/2 \\):\n     \\[\n     x_1 = \\frac{\\pi}{6}, \\quad x_{n+1} = x_n + \\frac{\\pi}{2}\n     \\]\n   - The sequence \\( x_n \\) modulo \\( \\pi \\) (due to periodicity) is periodic with period 4:\n     \\[\n     x_1 = \\frac{\\pi}{6}, \\quad x_2 = \\frac{2\\pi}{3}, \\quad x_3 = \\frac{7\\pi}{6}, \\quad x_4 = \\frac{5\\pi}{3}, \\quad x_5 = \\frac{\\pi}{6} + 2\\pi, \\ldots\n     \\]\n\n2. **Evaluate \\( y_n \\)**:\n   - Calculate \\( y_n = f(x_n) \\):\n     \\[\n     y_1 = 2, \\quad y_2 = -2, \\quad y_3 = 2, \\quad y_4 = -2\n     \\]\n   - The sequence \\( y_n \\) alternates between 2 and -2 every term.\n\n3. **Sum the sequence**:\n   - The sum of every 4 terms is \\( 2 - 2 + 2 - 2 = 0 \\).\n   - For 2018 terms, there are 504 full periods (2016 terms) and 2 remaining terms:\n     \\[\n     y_1 + y_2 + \\cdots + y_{2018} = 504 \\times 0 + (2 - 2) = 0\n     \\]\n\n### Final Answers\n\n1. The intervals where \\( f(x) \\) is monotonically increasing are \\( \\boxed{\\left( \\frac{2\\pi}{3} + k\\pi, \\frac{7\\pi}{6} + k\\pi \\right)} \\) for all integers \\( k \\).\n\n2. The value of \\( y_{1} + y_{2} + \\cdots + y_{2018} \\) is \\( \\boxed{0} \\).", "ground_truth_solution": "\n**Given**: The function \\( f(x) = 2 \\cos x (\\cos x + \\sqrt{3} \\sin x) - 1 \\).\n\nWe'll solve the problem in two parts:\n\n#### Part 1: Determine the monotonic increasing intervals of \\( f(x) \\).\n\n1. **Simplify the function**:\n\n\\[ \nf(x) = 2 \\cos x (\\cos x + \\sqrt{3} \\sin x) - 1 \n\\]\n\\[ \n= 2 (\\cos^2 x + \\sqrt{3} \\cos x \\sin x) - 1 \n\\]\n\nUsing the double-angle identities \\(\\cos^2 x = \\frac{1 + \\cos 2x}{2}\\) and \\(\\cos x \\sin x = \\frac{\\sin 2x}{2}\\):\n\n2. **Substitute the double-angle identities**:\n\n\\[ \n\\cos^2 x = \\frac{1 + \\cos 2x}{2} \n\\]\n\\[ \n\\cos x \\sin x = \\frac{\\sin 2x}{2} \n\\]\n\n3. By substituting these identities, we get:\n\n\\[ \nf(x) = 2 \\left( \\frac{1 + \\cos 2x}{2} + \\sqrt{3} \\cdot \\frac{\\sin 2x}{2} \\right) - 1 \n\\]\n\\[ \n= 1 + \\cos 2x + \\sqrt{3} \\sin 2x - 1 \n\\]\n\\[ \n= \\cos 2x + \\sqrt{3} \\sin 2x \n\\]\n\n4. **Express \\( f(x) \\) in terms of a single sine function**:\n\nRecall that \\( \\cos A + \\sqrt{3} \\sin A \\) can be transformed using the angle addition formula for sine:\n\\[ \n\\cos 2x + \\sqrt{3} \\sin 2x = 2 \\sin \\left( 2x + \\frac{\\pi}{6} \\right) \n\\]\nThus,\n\\[ \nf(x) = 2 \\sin \\left( 2x + \\frac{\\pi}{6} \\right) \n\\]\n\n5. **Find the intervals where \\( f(x) \\) is monotonic increasing**:\n\nSince sine function \\(\\sin t\\) is increasing in the interval \\( \\left[-\\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right] \\):\n\n\\[\n2x + \\frac{\\pi}{6} \\in \\left[-\\frac{\\pi}{2} + 2k\\pi, \\frac{\\pi}{2} + 2k\\pi\\right] \n\\]\n\n6. Solve for \\( x \\):\n\n\\[\n-\\frac{\\pi}{2} + 2k\\pi \\leq 2x + \\frac{\\pi}{6} \\leq \\frac{\\pi}{2} + 2k\\pi \n\\]\n\\[\n-\\frac{\\pi}{2} - \\frac{\\pi}{6} + 2k\\pi \\leq 2x \\leq \\frac{\\pi}{2} - \\frac{\\pi}{6} + 2k\\pi \n\\]\n\\[\n-\\frac{2\\pi}{3} + 2k\\pi \\leq 2x \\leq \\frac{\\pi}{3} + 2k\\pi \n\\]\n\\[\n-\\frac{\\pi}{3} + k\\pi \\leq x \\leq \\frac{\\pi}{6} + k\\pi \n\\]\n\nTherefore, the monotonic increasing intervals of \\( f(x) \\) are:\n\\[ \n\\left[-\\frac{\\pi}{3} + k\\pi, \\frac{\\pi}{6} + k\\pi \\right], \\quad k \\in \\mathbb{Z} \n\\]\n\n#### Part 2: Calculate \\( y_1 + y_2 + \\cdots + y_{2018} \\).\n\nGiven:\n\\[ \nx_1 = \\frac{\\pi}{6}, \\quad x_{n+1} - x_n = \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\quad (n \\in \\mathbb{N}^*) \n\\]\n\n1. **Define \\( t_n \\) and find its general form**:\n\nLet:\n\\[ \nt_n = 2x_n + \\frac{\\pi}{6} \n\\]\nFor \\( n = 1 \\):\n\\[ \nt_1 = 2x_1 + \\frac{\\pi}{6} = 2 \\cdot \\frac{\\pi}{6} + \\frac{\\pi}{6} = \\frac{\\pi}{2} \n\\]\n\nSince \\( x_{n+1} = x_n + \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\):\n\\[ \nt_{n+1} = 2x_{n+1} + \\frac{\\pi}{6} = 2 \\left( x_n + \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right) + \\frac{\\pi}{6} = 2x_n + \\pi + \\frac{\\pi}{6} = t_n + \\pi 