\\), lying in the \\(\\frac{n+1}{2}\\)-th segment.\n   - The endpoints of this segment are \\(D\\) and \\(E\\) with coordinates:\n     - \\(D: \\left( \\frac{c(n-1)}{2n}, \\frac{b(n+1)}{2n} \\right)\\)\n     - \\(E: \\left( \\frac{c(n+1)}{2n}, \\frac{b(n-1)}{2n} \\right)\\)\n\n4. **Slopes of \\(AD\\) and \\(AE\\)**:\n   - Slope of \\(AD\\): \\(\\frac{b(n+1)/2n}{c(n-1)/2n} = \\frac{b(n+1)}{c(n-1)}\\)\n   - Slope of \\(AE\\): \\(\\frac{b(n-1)/2n}{c(n+1)/2n} = \\frac{b(n-1)}{c(n+1)}\\)\n\n5. **Tangent of the Angle**:\n   - Using the formula for the tangent of the angle between two lines with slopes \\(m_1\\) and \\(m_2\\):\n     \\[\n     \\tan \\alpha = \\left| \\frac{m_2 - m_1}{1 + m_1 m_2} \\right|\n     \\]\n   - Substituting \\(m_1\\) and \\(m_2\\):\n     \\[\n     \\tan \\alpha = \\left| \\frac{\\frac{b(n-1)}{c(n+1)} - \\frac{b(n+1)}{c(n-1)}}{1 + \\frac{b(n+1)}{c(n-1)} \\cdot \\frac{b(n-1)}{c(n+1)}} \\right|\n     \\]\n   - Simplifying the numerator and denominator:\n     - Numerator: \\(\\frac{b}{c} \\cdot \\frac{(n-1)^2 - (n+1)^2}{(n+1)(n-1)} = \\frac{b}{c} \\cdot \\frac{-4n}{n^2 - 1}\\)\n     - Denominator: \\(1 + \\frac{b^2}{c^2} = \\frac{a^2}{c^2}\\)\n   - Combining and simplifying using \\(h = \\frac{bc}{a}\\):\n     \\[\n     \\tan \\alpha = \\frac{4n \\cdot \\frac{bc}{a}}{(n^2 - 1)a} = \\frac{4nh}{(n^2 - 1)a}\n     \\]\n\nThus, the final result is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\operatorname{tg} \\alpha = \\dfrac{4nh}{(n^2 - 1)a}}\n\\]", "ground_truth_solution": "Let's consider right triangle \\( ABC \\) with \\( BC = a \\) as the hypotenuse divided into \\( n \\) equal segments, where \\( n \\) is any odd natural number. Let \\( h \\) be the height corresponding to the hypotenuse and \\( \\alpha \\) be the angle at vertex \\( A \\) from which the midpoint of segment \\( PQ \\) containing midpoint \\( F \\) of the hypotenuse is observed.\n\n#### Step-by-Step Solution:\n1. **Setup Segment Length:**\n   Let the points on the hypotenuse \\( BC \\) in the order \\( B, P, F,